We are given $N$ mochi with sizes $A_1, A_2, \dots, A_N$.
The mochi are sorted in ascending order, i.e., $A_1 \le A_2 \le \dots \le A_N$.
The condition for placing mochi $A$ on top of mochi $B$ is $a \le \frac{b}{2}$, where $a$ is the size of the top mochi and $b$ is the size of the bottom mochi.
This inequality can be rewritten as $2a \le b$.

We need to count the number of pairs of indices $(i, j)$ such that $1 \le i, j \le N$, $i \neq j$, and $A_i$ is placed on top of $A_j$.
